## 🔌 INTEGRACJE

### 1. Open-Meteo API (Darmowe)

**Endpoint:**
```
https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast
```

**Request:**
```typescript
const response = await fetch(
  `https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?` +
  `latitude=${lat}&longitude=${lng}&` +
  `current_weather=true&` +
  `hourly=temperature_2m,relative_humidity_2m,precipitation,pressure_msl,cloud_cover,wind_speed_10m,wind_direction_10m`
);
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "current_weather": {
    "temperature": 15.5,
    "windspeed": 12.3,
    "winddirection": 270,
    "weathercode": 2,
    "time": "2025-11-01T12:00"
  },
  "hourly": {
    "temperature_2m": [14.2, 15.1, ...],
    "pressure_msl": [1013, 1012, ...],
    ...
  }
}
```

### 2. Netatmo OAuth API (Opcjonalne)

**Wymagania:**
- Client ID
- Client Secret
- Redirect URI
- Scopes: `read_station`

**Flow:**
1. Admin konfiguruje credentials w Admin Panel
2. User authorize przez Netatmo OAuth
3. Edge Function `netatmo-oauth-callback` receives code
4. Exchange code for tokens
5. Store tokens w `weather_oauth_config`
6. Cron job (`netatmo-refresh-token`) refreshes co 50 min
7. Edge Function `netatmo-weather-data` fetches weather

**Edge Functions:**

**netatmo-oauth-callback/index.ts:**
```typescript
import { serve } from "https://deno.land/std@0.168.0/http/server.ts";
import { createClient } from "https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2";

serve(async (req) => {
  const url = new URL(req.url);
  const code = url.searchParams.get('code');

  // Exchange code for tokens
  const tokenResponse = await fetch('https://api.netatmo.com/oauth2/token', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
    body: new URLSearchParams({
      grant_type: 'authorization_code',
      client_id: Deno.env.get('NETATMO_CLIENT_ID'),
      client_secret: Deno.env.get('NETATMO_CLIENT_SECRET'),
      code: code,
      redirect_uri: Deno.env.get('NETATMO_REDIRECT_URI')
    })
  });

  const tokens = await tokenResponse.json();

  // Save tokens to database
  const supabase = createClient(
    Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_URL'),
    Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY')
  );

  await supabase
    .from('weather_oauth_config')
    .update({
      access_token: tokens.access_token,
      refresh_token: tokens.refresh_token,
      token_expires_at: new Date(Date.now() + tokens.expires_in * 1000),
      is_configured: true
    })
    .eq('provider_id', '...');

  return new Response('Success! You can close this window.', { status: 200 });
});
```

**netatmo-refresh-token/index.ts:**
```typescript
// Cron job co 50 minut
// Refreshes access token using refresh token
```

**netatmo-weather-data/index.ts:**
```typescript
// Pobiera aktualne dane pogodowe z Netatmo
// GET /functions/v1/netatmo-weather-data?lat=52.2&lng=21.0
```

### 3. Supabase Storage (Zdjęcia ryb)

**Bucket:** `fish-images`

**Upload:**
```typescript
const file = event.target.files[0];
const fileName = `${userId}/${sessionId}/${catchId}_${Date.now()}.jpg`;

const { data, error } = await supabase.storage
  .from('fish-images')
  .upload(fileName, file, {
    cacheControl: '3600',
    upsert: false
  });

if (data) {
  const publicURL = supabase.storage
    .from('fish-images')
    .getPublicUrl(fileName).data.publicUrl;

  // Save publicURL to catch.photo_urls[]
}
```

**RLS Policy:**
```sql
-- Users can upload only to their own folder
CREATE POLICY "Users can upload own images"
ON storage.objects FOR INSERT
TO authenticated
WITH CHECK (
  bucket_id = 'fish-images' AND
  (storage.foldername(name))[1] = auth.uid()::text
);

-- Users can view only their own images
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own images"
ON storage.objects FOR SELECT
TO authenticated
USING (
  bucket_id = 'fish-images' AND
  (storage.foldername(name))[1] = auth.uid()::text
);
```

