## 🔒 BEZPIECZEŃSTWO

### Row Level Security (RLS)

**ZAWSZE włącz RLS dla każdej tabeli!**

```sql
ALTER TABLE table_name ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
```

**Przykładowe policies:**

```sql
-- Users can view only their own data
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own sessions"
ON fishing_sessions FOR SELECT
TO authenticated
USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Users can insert only their own data
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own sessions"
ON fishing_sessions FOR INSERT
TO authenticated
WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Users can update only their own data
CREATE POLICY "Users can update own sessions"
ON fishing_sessions FOR UPDATE
TO authenticated
USING (auth.uid() = user_id)
WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Users can delete only their own data
CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own sessions"
ON fishing_sessions FOR DELETE
TO authenticated
USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Admins can view all data
CREATE POLICY "Admins can view all sessions"
ON fishing_sessions FOR SELECT
TO authenticated
USING (
  EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM user_profiles
    WHERE user_profiles.id = auth.uid()
    AND user_profiles.role = 'admin'
  )
);
```

### Best Practices

1. **NIGDY nie wył RLS** na tabelach z danymi użytkowników
2. **Zawsze sprawdzaj** `auth.uid()` w policies
3. **Używaj funkcji pomocniczych** dla complex policies
4. **Test policies** z różnymi rolami użytkowników
5. **Nie przechowuj secrets** w frontend code
6. **Używaj Service Role Key** tylko w Edge Functions
7. **Waliduj input** na frontend i backend
8. **Rate limiting** dla API endpoints
9. **CORS** - only allowed origins
10. **HTTPS** - zawsze w production

